{"ts":"2026-07-25T07:12:47.068Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-25T07:12:47.068Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-07-25T07:12:47.062Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Duplicate-check evidence (all-status pm search over unknown subcommand, suggested_retry, did-you-mean, positional, recovery): matched closed pm-8nyc, pm-r2kd, pm-bu1m, pm-zwl7 and open pm-g543, pm-gdi7, pm-ulqu, pm-mpbb. pm-g543 is top-level command ranking, pm-gdi7 is unknown-option suggestion, pm-ulqu is enum value-domain rendering inside an existing suggested_retry, pm-r2kd was a single command silently falling back to list. None covers positional subcommand tokens across families. Filed as a child of pm-mpbb."}]}],"before_hash":"5323b48772badce8db1b634b44e69c3b0ef3a2d985be335c4e0a78f4b2680baa","after_hash":"af7c20d5b9be828d803c3f611280ce2a50b8ea1dd921d3d3b5cf162ed60c0a06"}
{"ts":"2026-07-25T07:12:48.042Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-07-25T07:12:48.039Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Reproduction on 2026.7.25, exact --json .code values: pm schema add-typ Foo -> unknown_subcommand (detail carries the full 15-token allowed set; title truncates it mid-list with an ellipsis). pm graph analyz -> invalid_argument_value (allowed set present in detail). pm plan sttus -> command_failed (allowed set present in detail; the code says execution failure for what is an input error). pm schema add type Foo -> invalid_command_usage with detail 'error: too many arguments for schema. Expected 2 arguments but got 3: add, type, Foo' and no allowed set at all. None of the four returns suggested_retry, although each mistake is edit distance 1 (or a pure hyphenation difference) from a valid token and the allowed set is available at the failure site. The space-form trap is invited by pm schema --help, which renders the subcommand list as 'add/remove type/status/field' rather than the literal tokens add-type, add-status, add-field, remove-type, remove-field."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-07-25T07:12:48.042Z"}],"before_hash":"af7c20d5b9be828d803c3f611280ce2a50b8ea1dd921d3d3b5cf162ed60c0a06","after_hash":"527cc7202d6f6f8b9be2b6cd6aae2554f31f77b9f1b5f1e931400053cf674fc2"}
